  "term": "KOR",
  "definition": "KOR refers to the kappa opioid receptor, a receptor in the brain whose activation is linked to the unpleasant or aversive effects of stress. In the source, KOR activity is described as shaping neural circuits involved in neurobehavioral disorders and as directly inhibiting dopamine-producing neurons in the ventral tegmental area.",
